course: dictionary
lesson: 12614
title: Discrete: separate and countable
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: «Discrete» means separate and distinct: each part is clearly apart from the others. Think of three separate piles of books, with a gap between each pile. «The shelves hold three discrete piles of books.» Each pile stands alone.
explain: In maths, discrete data are the things you count, like «the number of pets in a house». You can have 0, 1, 2 or 3 pets, but never 1.5 pets. Discrete data jump from one value to the next, usually whole numbers.
explain: Check with a swap. Put your meaning into the sentence: «The shelves hold three separate piles of books.» If it still makes sense, your meaning is right. Discrete is a long word, but the idea is simple: separate, and countable.
fact: «Discrete» means separate and distinct, with clear gaps between the parts.
fact: In maths, «discrete data» can only take certain values, usually whole numbers that you count.
fact: Things you count, like shoes, goals or children, are discrete. Things you measure, like height or time, are not.
fact: In science, «discrete steps» are clear, separate steps that happen one after another.
fact: Remember: discrete means separate and countable. It does not mean the same as «discreet», which means careful not to be noticed.
exercise: «The three rooms are discrete, each with its own door.» What does discrete mean here? | Round and smooth | Joined together with no gaps | *Separate and clearly apart | Very loud
exercise: Which of these is discrete data? | Time taken to run a race | *The number of pets in each house | The temperature of the sea | Height of the children
exercise: «The science lesson had discrete steps: first mix, then heat, then cool.» Find and copy the word that means clearly separate. | heat | *discrete | cool | mix
test: «We counted discrete data: 4 goals, 7 goals, 2 goals.» Why is this discrete? | Goals are measured with a ruler | Goals can be any length | Goals are always wet | *Goals are whole numbers that you count
test: Which one is NOT discrete data? | Number of shoes | Number of children | *Height of a tree | Number of books
exam: What does «discrete» mean in «The three parts of the model are discrete»? | Hard to see | *Separate and clearly apart from each other | Very, very cold | Joined together with no gaps
